WEBVTT
NOTE SYNTHETIC_PILOT — Instructor-authored demonstration transcript for M1.
NOTE Not a real stakeholder interview. All speech is fictionalized for tooling tests.

cue-0001
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:08.000
<v interviewer>Thanks for meeting. Can you describe how lecturers book library workshops today?

cue-0002
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:17.000
<v coordinator>Right now they email me. I check the room calendar and reply if the slot works.

cue-0003
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:26.000
<v coordinator>Lecturers should be able to request a workshop booking for their class online instead of emailing.

cue-0004
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:35.000
<v coordinator>I need the course code, expected headcount, preferred date, and which resources they want covered.

cue-0005
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:44.000
<v coordinator>If two classes want the same slot, the earlier request should win unless I override for a larger cohort.

cue-0006
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:52.000
<v lecturer>I also need a confirmation I can show students, and a way to cancel if the class is moved.

cue-0007
00:00:52.500 --> 00:01:01.000
<v coordinator>Cancellations happen, but we never wrote down how late they can cancel. That is still fuzzy.

cue-0008
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:10.000
Administrator: Rooms are capped; we should not overbook capacity even if a lecturer insists.
